{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 6, :comments ["<b>And the sabbath of the land shall be unto you for food</b> — Since He said (Leviticus 25:4), \"A sabbath of solemn rest it shall be for the land,\" He now says that the cessation mentioned shall be unto you for food, and you shall all live from it — you and your servant and your beast and the wild animal — that you shall all live from what the land produces of itself during its cessation. Or perhaps the year is called \"the sabbath of the land\" just as the day is called the sabbath of YHWH and simply \"sabbath,\" and the meaning concerns the produce of the sabbath, for the sabbath itself cannot be eaten."], :book :leviticus, :voice :ramban, :lang :en, :chapter 25, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T03:59:23.020588958Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}